Top 10 Stock Exchanges by Market Capitalization
Global stock exchanges are ranked below by their total market value in US dollars: 

* 1. New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) – USA (~$31 trillion)
The top US exchange for traditional blue-chip and massive global companies.
* 2. NASDAQ – USA (~$28 trillion)
The leading home for major tech giants like Apple, Microsoft, and Amazon.
* 3. Shanghai Stock Exchange (SSE) – China (~$10 trillion)
The largest mainland Chinese stock exchange.
*  4. Euronext – Pan-Europe (~$8.7 trillion)
A major cross-border European exchange operating across multiple countries.
*   5. Japan Exchange Group (JPX) / Tokyo Stock Exchange – Japan (~$7.6 trillion)
The premier financial market hub in Japan.
*   6. Hong Kong Stock Exchange (HKEX) – Hong Kong (~$7 trillion)
A vital gateway linking international investors with Chinese equities.
* 7. London Stock Exchange (LSE) – United Kingdom (~$6.6 trillion)
Europe's leading historical venue for international finance.
*  8. Shenzhen Stock Exchange (SZSE) – China (~$4.5 trillion)
China's second major mainland exchange focused heavily on growing tech and entrepreneurial companies.
*  9. TMX Group / Toronto Stock Exchange – Canada (~$2.8 trillion)
